        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fetch MiniMax Token Plan recharge credit balance",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- MiniMax Coding Plan / Token Plan **remains APIs do not expose the console recharge-credit balance** (积分余额). CodexBar now fetches it from the web console endpoint `GET /backend/account/token_plan_credit` on `www.minimaxi.com` / `www.minimax.io` when a browser session cookie is available.\n- Web-session refreshes always attempt the credit fetch after quota/billing enrichment (even when billing history is disabled).\n- API-token refreshes also merge the credit balance when a manual/env/cached cookie is present, so `sk-cp-*` users can see both quota and recharge credits without switching source mode.\n- Credit enrichment is best-effort: auth/transport failures leave the quota snapshot intact instead of failing the whole provider.\n- Diagnostics export now includes `pointsBalance`; menu rendering reuses the existing `MiniMax points balance` cost row.\n\n## Motivation\n\nUsers with recharge credits (e.g. 20,000 points in the MiniMax console) saw quota data via API key but `providerCostPresent: false` in diagnostics and no balance in the menu. The balance lives on a separate cookie-authenticated endpoint discovered from the platform web bundle.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `swift test --filter MiniMaxTokenPlanCreditTests`\n- [x] `make check`\n- [x] Parser coverage for `remaining_credits`, `balance_breakdown.total_balance`, and `total_credits - used_credits`\n- [x] Web + API enrichment paths via `ProviderHTTPTransportStub`\n- [x] Region/override URL tests and diagnostic mapping test\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Bearer API key alone still cannot read `token_plan_credit` (console returns `not login`); cookie is required for the balance.\n- Optional override: `MINIMAX_TOKEN_PLAN_CREDIT_URL`\n- Docs: `docs/minimax.md`\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
        "branch": "feat/minimax-token-plan-credit",
